{
  "title": "Dua for Fending Off Distress, Grief, and Fear",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "يَا اَبْصَرَ النَّاظِرِيْنَ\nYAA ABSARAN NAAZIREEN\nO Most Seeing of seers,\nيَا اَسْمَعَ السَّامِعِيْنَ\nYAA ASMA-A'S SAAMI-E'EN\nO Most Hearing of hearers,\nيَا اَسْرَعَ الْحَاسِبِيْنَ\nYAA ASRA-A'L HAASIBEEN\nO Swiftest of reckoners,\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO Most Merciful of the merciful.",
  "merits": "Imam al-Baqir (a.s.) said: whenever a horrifying matter befalls you, turn toward the qiblah and offer a two-unit prayer. Once done, say this supplication seventy times, submitting your request each time you reach its end."
}
